From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:50:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] greeter: mouse focus, a Log in button and a power menu

A click in an input field gives it the keys.  loginButtonLabel adds a
Log in button (activeColor) under the right edge of the fields: with no
name yet it gives the name field the keys, else it submits like Enter in
the last field.  rebootCommand and shutdownCommand add a Power button on
the left that opens a menu of rebootLabel and shutdownLabel upwards over
the box (menuColor, the entry under the pointer in activeColor); a click
runs the command through the shell, detached; a click outside the menu
or any key closes it.  The box grows by the row of buttons, and clearing
the failure message leaves them alone.
---
